---
/**
 * Full Mouth Dental Implants — Vivid Smiles Dentistry, Parker CO.
 * Page-scoped styles: src/styles/pages/full-mouth-dental-implants.css (.fmdi wrapper).
 *
 * Recipe: All-on-4 single-arch template, namespace .fmdi, copy mapped
 * verbatim from the SEO brief. Adaptations vs. the source recipe:
 *   - "What" cream split has NO sub-grid (the brief's only definition-level copy is
 *     a single short paragraph; the original Upper-vs-Lower split has no analog).
 *   - "Benefits" paper grid is a 4-card mapping of the verbatim
 *     "How Full Mouth Implants Differ from Traditional Dentures" bullets,
 *     replacing the all-on-4 "Living" (Eating/Cleaning/etc.) cards since the
 *     brief has no daily-life copy.
 *   - "Compare" sub-grid is 2 alternatives instead of 3 (the brief lists 4
 *     options total; 2 occupy the head-to-head, 2 occupy the sub).
 *   - 6 FAQs (vs. 8 in all-on-4) per brief.
 *
 * MIGRATED TO BLOCKS (docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md 2.3). Ten top-level bands — why,
 * what, robotics, process, compare, candidacy, benefits, cost, gallery, faq —
 * each guarded with `hasBlocks ? null : …` and each carrying a row in
 * cms/import/block-map.json under /implant-dentistry/full-mouth-dental-implants/.
 * The map value under review lives at cms/import/routes/full-mouth-dental-implants.json.
 *
 * NO <LocalTrust> ON THIS PAGE, so no `code_section` row, and nothing here
 * touches cms/mu-plugins/vs-content-model.php or CodeSectionBlock.astro.
 *
 * THE BAND NAMES IN THE SECTION COMMENTS BELOW WERE WRONG AND ARE CORRECTED IN
 * PLACE. Three of them said "cream" and "sage" while
 * src/styles/pages/full-mouth-dental-implants.css has always painted
 * `.fmdi .section.alt` charcoal (:228) and `.fmdi .section.dark` sage-pale
 * (:238). The `band` value on every row of the map is read off those two rules,
 * not off the class name and not off the comment that used to sit above it —
 * copying a sibling page's vocabulary here would repaint five of these ten
 * bands, because `.section.alt` is cream on teeth-whitening.css:237.
 *
 * Three things this page owns that neither worked example does, all three
 * recorded as known_gaps on their block in the map rather than closed here:
 *   1. `#robotics` is a bespoke `.robotics-grid` whose callout is
 *      `.label` + `<h4>` + `<p>`; media_split draws `.natural-*` and an
 *      `<aside class="veneers-callout">` with an `<h3>` and no label slot.
 *   2. `#compare` is TWO shapes in one band — two `.compare-card`s carrying
 *      `.compare-list` bullets, plus a `.compare-sub` head over an
 *      `.alternatives-grid` of two `.config-card`s. `comparison_cards` has one
 *      card list and one aside, so the sub-grid has nowhere to go.
 *   3. `#candidacy`'s `.candidate-list` IS what media_split's `checklist`
 *      repeater now draws, markers derived from row position — the one shape on
 *      this page that a recently added field carries exactly.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import FinalBand from '../../components/FinalBand.astro';
import VirtualConsult from '../../components/VirtualConsult.astro';
import PricingTiers from '../../components/PricingTiers.astro';
import { phoneHref, phoneLabel, bookNowHref } from '../../data/contact';
import { getSmiles } from '../../lib/smiles';
import '../../styles/pages/full-mouth-dental-implants.css';

// "What is full-mouth implants" — a real full-arch restoration on a lab
// model: the whole-arch prosthesis this page is about, shown as an object
// rather than as a patient's result.
// Robotics section — keep the authentic Dr. Bryce Yomi-guided procedure.
// Candidacy — lifestyle patient portrait.
import { getPageContent, type TocLink } from '../../lib/page-content';
import PageBlocks from '../../blocks/PageBlocks.astro';
// tocLinks, processSteps, faqs are edited in WordPress (Pages -> Full Mouth Dental Implants in Parker, CO).
// The shapes are unchanged from the arrays that used to live here, so the
// markup below is untouched.
const { blocks, hasBlocks, tocLinks, processSteps, faqs, section, image, seo } =
  await getPageContent(Astro.url.pathname);


// Track doubled for seamless marquee loop.
const galleryTiles = getSmiles();
const galleryTrack = [...galleryTiles, ...galleryTiles];

const whyCards = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Implant Pathway · 600+ hours',
    body: 'Dr. Richardson was part of the staff at Implant Pathway, accumulating 600+ hours of surgical training. That places him in a small tier of general dentists at this level.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Robotic-guided placement',
    body: 'Robotic-assisted surgery improves placement accuracy to within fractions of a millimeter, which matters most in full arch cases where four to six implants must support a bridge and placement errors compound across the arch.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'In-house milling & 3D printing',
    body: 'His in-house lab includes milling units and 3D printers for prosthetic fabrication, keeping quality control with the surgeon throughout.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: '300+ reviews · Parker roots',
    body: 'With over 300 five-star Google reviews and deep Parker roots, he brings destination-level full arch expertise to a neighborhood practice.',
  },
];

const benefitCards = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Bone preservation',
    body: 'Implants transfer chewing forces into the jawbone, preventing the resorption that dentures accelerate.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Stability',
    body: 'The bridge is fixed to the implants; no adhesive, shifting, or daily removal.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Diet',
    body: 'No food restrictions; full arch implant patients eat normally, including hard and chewy foods.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Facial structure',
    body: 'The jaw retains its density, so the face maintains its shape rather than developing the sunken look common in long-term denture wearers.',
  },
];

const alternatives = [
  {
    tag: 'Alternative',
    title: 'Implant-supported overdentures',
    body: 'More stable than conventional dentures with two to four implant attachments, but still removable and do not stop bone loss.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Alternative',
    title: 'Individual implants per tooth',
    body: 'Clinically appropriate for isolated losses; impractical and overly complex for full arch tooth loss.',
  },
];

const keyStats: [string, string][] = [
  ['4–6', 'Implants Per Arch'],
  ['Same-Day', 'Temporary Teeth'],
  ['4–9 mo', 'Treatment Time'],
  ['20+ yrs', 'Prosthetic Bridge'],
];

/**
 * The "On this page" rail, derived from the blocks themselves (docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md 1.2).
 *
 * Used only when this page renders from `blocks`. The `toc_links` repeater is
 * nine rows that restate the order of the ten bands below it, so a reorder in
 * wp-admin moves a band and leaves its rail entry pointing at the old
 * neighbour — the single largest way a reorder breaks a link. Reading the
 * anchors off the blocks makes that unrepresentable: there is one ordering and
 * the rail is a projection of it.
 *
 * Three rules, in the order they bite:
 *
 * 1. A blank anchor is skipped. Not tidiness — src/scripts/toc-spy.ts:24 feeds
 *    each rendered href straight to document.querySelector(), and
 *    querySelector("") throws a SyntaxError that kills the whole spy, not just
 *    the one entry. PageBlocks.astro emits no id at all for a blank anchor
 *    (`id={anchor || undefined}`), so there is nothing to link to either.
 * 2. An anchor that is not a valid id selector is skipped for the same reason —
 *    "#3-reasons" is legal HTML and an illegal CSS selector. Dropping one rail
 *    entry costs one link; letting it through costs every link on the page,
 *    plus the mobile pill auto-centering.
 * 3. Duplicate anchors follow PageBlocks.astro's dedup exactly, second
 *    occurrence onward suffixed `-2`, `-3`. The counter has to advance on every
 *    non-blank anchor, including blocks with no nav_label, or the rail's idea
 *    of "the second #faq" drifts from the id the renderer actually emitted.
 *
 * A blank nav_label means "leave this block out of the rail" (1.2), which is
 * how a band that should not be navigable opts out — `gallery` on this page,
 * which has no toc_links row and never appeared in the rail.
 */
const ANCHOR_IS_ID_SELECTOR = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/;

const anchorsSeen = new Map<string, number>();
// Typed as TocLink[] rather than an equivalent inline shape so the ternary in
// the rail below collapses to one type instead of a union of two array types,
// which TypeScript will not let you call .map() on.
const derivedTocLinks: TocLink[] = [];

for (const block of blocks) {
  const anchor = typeof block.anchor === 'string' ? block.anchor.trim() : '';
  if (anchor === '') continue;

  const nth = (anchorsSeen.get(anchor) ?? 0) + 1;
  anchorsSeen.set(anchor, nth);

  const label = typeof block.navLabel === 'string' ? block.navLabel.trim() : '';
  if (label === '') continue;

  if (!ANCHOR_IS_ID_SELECTOR.test(anchor)) {
    console.warn(
      `[blocks] anchor "${anchor}" on ${Astro.url.pathname} cannot be used as a selector — ` +
        `omitting "${label}" from the On this page rail so toc-spy keeps working`,
    );
    continue;
  }

  derivedTocLinks.push({ href: `#${nth > 1 ? `${anchor}-${nth}` : anchor}`, label });
}

---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title || "Full Mouth Dental Implants in Parker, CO | Vivid Smiles Dentistry"}
  description={seo.description || "Full mouth dental implants in Parker, CO with Dr. Bryce Richardson — robotic placement, CBCT planning, four-to-six titanium implants per arch with a fixed bridge. Free consultation."}
 noindex={seo.noindex}>
  <div class="fmdi">
    {/* ---------- BREADCRUMB ---------- */}
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <div class="crumbs-inner">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="/services/">Services</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <a href="/implant-dentistry/">Implant Dentistry</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span class="here">Full Mouth Dental Implants</span>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main id="main">
      {/* ---------- HERO ---------- */}
      <header class="hero" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap hero-inner">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">Implant Dentistry · Parker, CO</span>
            <h1 data-vs-reveal-lines>Full Mouth Dental Implants <em>in Parker, Colorado</em></h1>
            <p class="hero-sub">
              Full mouth dental implants replace an entire arch with a fixed, non-removable
              prosthesis supported by four to six titanium implants fused to the jaw. They function
              like natural teeth and preserve the bone that traditional dentures allow to erode.
              Below is what the procedure involves, who qualifies, and what to expect at Vivid
              Smiles Dentistry.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <Button variant="light" href={bookNowHref} hoverLabel="Let's Talk">Book Online</Button
              >
              <Button variant="ghost-light" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video"
                >Free Virtual Consult</Button
              >
              <div class="ratings">
                <span class="stars" aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</span>
                <span>5.0 · 300+ reviews</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-img" data-vs-parallax data-parallax="-30">
            <Image
              src={image("heroImg").url} width={image("heroImg").width} height={image("heroImg").height}
              alt="Smiling woman photographed inside the Vivid Smiles Dentistry office in Parker, CO"
              widths={[600, 900, 1400]}
              sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw"
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      {/* ---------- KEYS — at-a-glance ---------- */}
      <section
        class="keys"
        id="keys"
        aria-label="Full mouth dental implants at a glance"
        data-vs-reveal-batch
      >
        <div class="keys-grid">
          <div class="keys-label">At a glance</div>
          {
            keyStats.map(([k, v]) => (
              <div class="keys-item">
                <>
                  <div class="k">{k}</div>
                  <div class="v">{v}</div>
                </>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      {
        /* ---------- ON-THIS-PAGE TOC ----------
         The rail itself is never a block (spec 7: "Not a block, even though it
         is a band") — only its contents move. Derived from the blocks when
         they are drawing the page, read from the `toc_links` repeater when the
         template is. Same markup either way, which is what lets
         src/scripts/toc-spy.ts go on reading its section list off the rendered
         links without knowing which source produced them. */
      }
      <nav class="toc" id="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <div class="toc-inner">
          <span class="toc-label">On this page</span>
          <div class="toc-scroll">
            <div class="toc-list">
              {(hasBlocks ? derivedTocLinks : tocLinks).map((l) => <a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>)}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </nav>

      {
        /* ---------- WHY (paper, 4-card grid) ----------

         THE MIGRATION SWITCH (docs/PAGE-BLOCKS.md 2.3) starts here. `hasBlocks`
         means "this build can draw this page from its blocks" — not "WordPress
         sent rows" (src/lib/page-content.ts). When it is true PageBlocks draws
         the ten bands in the order an editor arranged them; when it is false —
         which is every build until the backfill has run, and again the moment
         an editor empties the field — every band below renders exactly as it
         always has.

         Written as one guard per band rather than one guard around all ten on
         purpose, and it is not a style choice. Astro's compressHTML pass treats
         an Astro comment expression differently inside a component slot than at
         element level: wrapping these bands in a Fragment silently drops one
         space at every comment boundary below, and scripts/vr-html.mjs compares
         exact bytes and calls that a difference. A guard sitting exactly where
         its section sat emits byte-identical HTML.

         EVERY top-level band between here and <VirtualConsult> is guarded, and
         every one of them has a row in cms/import/block-map.json. Those two
         facts have to move together: a band that is neither blocked nor guarded
         renders in ADDITION to the block run and lands at the bottom of the
         page, and a band that is guarded with no map row disappears on backfill
         with nothing in the log. There is no third outcome. The bands ABOVE
         this line — the breadcrumb, the hero, `.keys` and the rail — are not
         blocks by spec 7 and are deliberately unguarded, as are <VirtualConsult>
         and <FinalBand> below the run.

         `.fmdi .section` (full-mouth-dental-implants.css:227) sets padding and
         nothing else, so this band is paper. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? <PageBlocks blocks={blocks} /> : <section class="section" id="why" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">{section("why").eyebrow}</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("why").heading} /></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="why-grid">
            {
              whyCards.map((c) => (
                <article class="why-card">
                  <div class="num">{c.num}</div>
                  <h3>{c.title}</h3>
                  <p>{c.body}</p>
                </article>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- WHAT (CHARCOAL split, no sub-grid — single-paragraph
         definition only) ----------

         The comment here said "cream" and the page has never been cream.
         `.fmdi .section.alt { background: var(--vs-charcoal-green) }` at
         full-mouth-dental-implants.css:228, with h2 #fff at :232 and p
         rgba(255,255,255,0.85) at :236. Dark band, white type. The map's `band`
         value is read off that rule; on teeth-whitening.css:237 the identical
         class name is cream, which is why the class is never the evidence. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section alt" id="what" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="what-grid">
            <div class="what-img" data-vs-parallax data-parallax="-25">
              <Image
                src={image("whatImg").url} width={image("whatImg").width} height={image("whatImg").height}
                alt="Full-arch restoration on a dental model, held in a gloved hand"
                widths={[500, 800, 1100]}
                sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="what-text">
              <span class="eyebrow">{section("what").eyebrow}</span>
              <h2><Fragment set:html={section("what").heading} /></h2>
              <div class="prose">
                <p>{section("what").body}</p>
              </div>
              <div class="cta-row left">
                <div class="cta-buttons">
                  <Button variant="light" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video"
                    >Free Virtual Consult</Button
                  >
                  <Button variant="ghost-light" href="#robotics" hoverLabel="See How"
                    >How It Works</Button
                  >
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- ROBOTICS (paper, with same-day callout) ----------
         `.fmdi .section` (full-mouth-dental-implants.css:227), no background
         rule, so the body paper shows through.

         THE BAND THIS PAGE LOSES THE MOST ON, and the loss is a layout fault
         rather than a copy fault. The markup below is a bespoke
         `.robotics-grid` / `.robotics-img` / `.robotics-text` family with a
         `<p class="robotics-prose">` and a `.robotics-callout` of
         `<span class="label">` + `<h4>` + `<p>`. media_split draws the
         `.natural-*` family, a `.prose > p`, and an
         `<aside class="veneers-callout">` of `<h3>` + `<p>`, with no slot for
         the label line. See `known_gaps` on this block in the route file for
         what exactly goes and what would close it; nothing is invented here to
         paper over it. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section" id="robotics" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="robotics-grid">
            <div class="robotics-img" data-vs-parallax data-parallax="-25">
              <Image
                src={image("roboticsImg").url} width={image("roboticsImg").width} height={image("roboticsImg").height}
                alt="Dr. Bryce Richardson placing a dental implant with the Yomi robotic arm at Vivid Smiles Dentistry"
                widths={[500, 800, 1100]}
                sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="robotics-text">
              <span class="eyebrow">{section("robotics").eyebrow}</span>
              <h2><Fragment set:html={section("robotics").heading} /></h2>
              <p class="robotics-prose">{section("robotics").body}</p>
              <div class="robotics-callout">
                <span class="label">Same-day teeth</span>
                <h4>Can You Get Teeth the Same Day?</h4>
                <p>
                  Many full arch patients receive a temporary prosthesis the same day as surgery.
                  The same-day restoration is a well-fitting temporary; the permanent bridge follows
                  after osseointegration is confirmed. Qualification depends on bone density and
                  implant stability achieved at surgery, both evaluated during your initial
                  consultation with Dr. Richardson.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- PROCESS (SAGE-PALE, 5-step recovery timeline +
         Advanced-Technology inline-cta) ----------

         The comment here said "sage" and the sheet says otherwise:
         `.fmdi .section.dark { background: var(--vs-sage-pale) }` at
         full-mouth-dental-implants.css:238, with h2 var(--vs-ink) at :242.
         `sage` and `sage-pale` are two separate BLOCK_BANDS choices painting
         two different tokens, so the map says sage-pale.

         Five steps in a five-column grid — `.fmdi .process-grid` is
         `repeat(5, 1fr)` at :441 — which the `columns` select now serves,
         because it gained a "5" choice. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section dark" id="process" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow light">Recovery Timeline</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("process").heading} /></h2>
            <p>{section("process").body}</p>
          </div>

          <div class="process-grid">
            {
              processSteps.map((s) => (
                <div class="process-card">
                  <span class="step-tag">{s.tag}</span>
                  <div class="num">{s.num}</div>
                  <h3>{s.title}</h3>
                  <p>{s.body}</p>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>

          <div class="inline-cta dark">
            <div class="ic-text">
              <strong>Advanced technology at Vivid Smiles.</strong> CBCT imaging maps nerve locations,
              bone quality, and implant trajectories before surgery begins, and digital smile design lets
              patients preview the result before committing to treatment. In-house milling and 3D printing
              produce prosthetic components, reducing appointments and keeping quality control with Dr.
              Richardson throughout the process.
            </div>
            <div class="ic-buttons">
              <Button variant="light" href={bookNowHref} hoverLabel="Let's Talk">Book Online</Button
              >
              <Button variant="ghost-light" href={phoneHref} hoverLabel="Tap to Dial"
                >Call {phoneLabel}</Button
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- COMPARE (paper, 1 featured + 1 main + 2-alt sub-grid) ----------
         `.fmdi .section` (full-mouth-dental-implants.css:227), no background
         rule, body paper.

         TWO SHAPES IN ONE BAND, and `comparison_cards` has room for one of
         them. The `.compare` head-to-head becomes the layout's `tiers`; the
         `.compare-sub` head becomes its `.safety-callout` aside, which is the
         one slot the layout has between the cards and the CTA row. The
         `.alternatives-grid` of two `.config-card`s has no slot at all — those
         two rows are the `alternatives` group in the CMS and are listed in
         `exempt.cards` in the route file rather than folded in among the
         head-to-head cards, because four peers is a different argument from two
         head-to-head plus two lesser options. Recorded as a known_gap with the
         field pair that would close it. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section" id="compare" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">{section("compare").eyebrow}</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("compare").heading} /></h2>
            <p>{section("compare").body}</p>
          </div>

          <div class="compare">
            <article class="compare-card featured">
              <span class="ribbon">Our Specialty</span>
              <span class="tag">Full Arch Implants</span>
              <h3>Full Arch Implants (All-on-4 / All-on-X)</h3>
              <ul class="compare-list">
                <li>
                  <b>Profile —</b> Fixed, bone-anchored, and designed for patients missing most or all
                  teeth in an arch.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <b>Implants —</b> Four to six titanium roots per arch supporting a non-removable bridge.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <b>Bone —</b> Transfers chewing forces into the jawbone, preventing the resorption that
                  dentures accelerate.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <b>Lifestyle —</b> No adhesive, shifting, or daily removal; no food restrictions once
                  healed.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <article class="compare-card">
              <span class="tag">Traditional Dentures</span>
              <h3>Traditional Dentures</h3>
              <ul class="compare-list">
                <li>
                  <b>Profile —</b> Removable, lower upfront cost, but permit ongoing bone resorption and
                  deteriorate in fit as the jaw changes shape.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <b>Bone —</b> Stay on top of the gums and allow the jawbone beneath them to shrink.
                </li>
                <li><b>Stability —</b> Require adhesive or daily removal and refitting.</li>
                <li>
                  <b>Lifestyle —</b> Restrict the diet and accelerate the sunken facial look common in
                  long-term denture wearers.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="compare-sub">
            <div class="compare-sub-head">
              <span class="eyebrow">Alternatives</span>
              <h3>Other Tooth-Replacement Options</h3>
              <div class="prose">
                <p>
                  Full-arch implants are the right call when most or all teeth in an arch are gone,
                  but other approaches fit different clinical pictures.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="alternatives-grid">
              {
                alternatives.map((a) => (
                  <article class="config-card">
                    <span class="tag">{a.tag}</span>
                    <h4>{a.title}</h4>
                    <p>{a.body}</p>
                  </article>
                ))
              }
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="cta-row">
            <div class="cta-buttons">
              <Button variant="sage" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video"
                >Free Virtual Consult</Button
              >
              <Button variant="ghost" href="#faq" hoverLabel="See Answers">Read FAQ</Button>
            </div>
            <span class="cta-note">No commitment · Personal video reply</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- CANDIDACY (CHARCOAL, image+text + "What If You Have Bone
         Loss?" sub) ----------

         Same `.fmdi .section.alt` rule as `what`,
         full-mouth-dental-implants.css:228 — charcoal, not the cream this
         comment used to claim.

         The band media_split fits best on this page: `.natural-grid` >
         `.natural-text` + `.natural-img` is character-for-character the family
         the block draws, and the `ul.candidate-list` under the pull quote is
         exactly what the `checklist` repeater now renders — `lead` carrying the
         bolded run and its em dash, the 01/02/03/04 markers DERIVED from row
         position rather than stored, which is why deleting a row here can never
         leave the list counting 01 03 04.

         The `.candidacy-sub` card below the grid is the part that does not fit:
         it becomes the aside inside the copy column. See the block's
         known_gaps. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section alt" id="candidacy" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="natural-grid">
            <div class="natural-text">
              <span class="eyebrow">Candidacy</span>
              <h2><Fragment set:html={section("candidacy").heading} /></h2>
              <div class="natural-quote">
                Full arch implants are for individuals missing most or all teeth in one or both
                arches, including those with severe decay, advanced gum disease, or long-term
                denture wearers seeking a permanent alternative.
              </div>
              <ul class="candidate-list">
                <li>
                  <span class="marker">01</span>
                  <span
                    ><b>Missing most or all teeth in an arch —</b> the procedure replaces every tooth
                    in one or both jaws with a fixed bridge.</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="marker">02</span>
                  <span
                    ><b>Severe decay or advanced gum disease —</b> failing teeth across the arch are removed
                    during the same surgical visit.</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="marker">03</span>
                  <span
                    ><b>Long-term denture wearers —</b> patients seeking a permanent alternative to removable
                    prosthetics.</span
                  >
                </li>
                <li>
                  <span class="marker">04</span>
                  <span
                    ><b>Most situations are treatable —</b> with the correct preparation, candidacy is
                    more inclusive than most patients expect.</span
                  >
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="natural-img" data-vs-parallax data-parallax="-25">
              <Image
                src={image("candidacyImg").url} width={image("candidacyImg").width} height={image("candidacyImg").height}
                alt="Woman seated in tall grass above a Colorado lake"
                widths={[500, 800, 1100]}
                sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, 50vw"
              />
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="candidacy-sub">
            <span class="label">If you have reduced bone</span>
            <h3>What If You Have Bone Loss?</h3>
            <p>{section("candidacy").body}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- BENEFITS (paper, 4-card — replaces all-on-4 "Living"; maps the
        verbatim Implants-vs-Dentures differences) ----------
        `.fmdi .section` (full-mouth-dental-implants.css:227), body paper. Four
        across: `.fmdi .benefits-grid` is `repeat(4, 1fr)` at :661, the same
        count `.fmdi .why-grid` carries at :278, so both card bands store
        columns "4". card_grid draws one card family — `.why-grid` /
        `.why-card` — so this band arrives under the `why` class names. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section" id="benefits" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">{section("benefits").eyebrow}</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("benefits").heading} /></h2>
            <p>{section("benefits").body}</p>
          </div>

          <div class="benefits-grid">
            {
              benefitCards.map((c) => (
                <article class="benefits-card">
                  <div class="num">{c.num}</div>
                  <h3>{c.title}</h3>
                  <p>{c.body}</p>
                </article>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- INVESTMENT (CHARCOAL) ----------
         Third band on this page carrying `.fmdi .section.alt`
         (full-mouth-dental-implants.css:228 -> var(--vs-charcoal-green)), and
         the comment above it said cream. Worth naming twice: porcelain-veneers'
         pricing band is PAPER and the note in its map entry says the implant
         family's are cream. Neither is this page. `band` is a field on the
         pricing_tiers layout precisely so it can be read off each sheet.

         A standalone <section> holding a `.section-head` and a one-tier
         <PricingTiers> — the shape the layout was built for, so nothing about
         this band needs a bespoke field. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section alt" id="cost" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">{section("cost").eyebrow}</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("cost").heading} /></h2>
            <p>{section("cost").body}</p>
          </div>

          <PricingTiers
            tiers={[
              {
                name: 'Full Mouth Dental Implants',
                priceQualifier: 'Starting at',
                price: '$19,995',
                priceSuffix: 'per arch',
                tagline: 'Full-arch fixed teeth — single arch or full mouth.',
                bullets: [
                  'Robotic implant placement per arch',
                  'Zirconia or acrylic prosthetic options',
                  'CBCT-planned with preparatory procedures included',
                  'PPO insurance benefits reviewed up front',
                  'In-house and third-party financing available',
                ],
                highlight: true,
                ribbon: 'Most Common',
              },
            ]}
            financingNote="Every case has a unique anatomy and material profile — a free consultation with CBCT imaging is the only way to get an accurate quote. Vivid Smiles works with third-party financing partners to spread the investment across monthly payments; patients without insurance can also enroll in the Vivid Smiles dental membership plan."
          />
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- GALLERY (sage-pale) — marquee, doubled track.
         Same `.fmdi .section.dark { background: var(--vs-sage-pale) }` rule as
         `process`, full-mouth-dental-implants.css:238.

         Out of the rail on both sides of the switch: this page has no
         `toc_links` row for #gallery — its nine rows are why, what, robotics,
         process, compare, candidacy, benefits, cost, faq — so the derived rail
         leaves it out exactly as the repeater does. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section dark" id="gallery">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head" data-vs-reveal>
            <span class="eyebrow light">Smile Gallery</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("gallery").heading} /></h2>
            <p>{section("gallery").body}</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="gallery-marquee" data-vs-marquee aria-label="Vivid Smiles smile gallery">
          <div class="gallery-track" data-vs-marquee-track>
            {
              galleryTrack.map((t, i) => {
                const isClone = i >= galleryTiles.length;
                return (
                  <div
                    class="smile-tile"
                    aria-hidden={isClone || undefined}
                    inert={isClone || undefined}
                  >
                    <Image src={t.src} width={t.width} height={t.height} alt={t.alt} widths={[420, 640, 840]} sizes="420px" />
                  </div>
                );
              })
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- FAQ (paper, 6 accordion items + closing pull-quote) ----------
         `.fmdi .section` (full-mouth-dental-implants.css:227), body paper.
         Native details/summary, zero JS.

         The answers are rendered `set:html` on both sides of the switch — one
         of these six carries two `<a class="vs-link">` tags, so the escaped
         path would print the markup at the patient. FaqBlock uses set:html for
         the same reason. */
      }
      {hasBlocks ? null : <section class="section" id="faq" data-vs-reveal-batch>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head">
            <span class="eyebrow">{section("faq").eyebrow}</span>
            <h2><Fragment set:html={section("faq").heading} /></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-list">
            {
              faqs.map((f) => (
                <details class="faq" open={f.open}>
                  <summary>
                    <>
                      <h3>{f.q}</h3>
                      <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        +
                      </span>
                    </>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="answer" set:html={f.a} />
                </details>
              ))
            }
          </div>

          <div class="pull">
            <p>{section("faq").body}</p>
          </div>

          <div class="cta-row">
            <div class="cta-buttons">
              <Button variant="sage" href="#consult" hoverLabel="Get a Video"
                >Still Have Questions? Free Virtual Consult</Button
              >
              <Button variant="ghost" href={phoneHref} hoverLabel="Tap to Dial"
                >Call {phoneLabel}</Button
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>}

      {
        /* ---------- VIRTUAL CONSULT — primary closing conversion.
         NOT a block and deliberately unguarded, like the breadcrumb, hero,
         `.keys` strip and the rail above: it renders on both sides of the
         switch and has no row in the map. It sits after the block run in
         template order and PageBlocks draws at the `why` position, so the
         closing pair still comes last.
         Anchor #consult is the destination for every mid-page CTA on this
         page. */
      }
      <VirtualConsult id="consult" eyebrow="Free full mouth implant consultation">
        <Fragment slot="headline">Free full mouth implant <em>consultation.</em></Fragment>
        <Fragment slot="body">
          Vivid Smiles Dentistry in Parker, CO, brings Dr. Richardson's 600+ hours of surgical
          training, Implant Pathway credentials, and robotic technology to deliver outcomes grounded
          in precision planning. Schedule your free consultation below or call {phoneLabel} to learn whether
          full-mouth implants are the right path for you.
        </Fragment>
      </VirtualConsult>

      {/* ---------- CLOSING BAND ---------- */}
      <FinalBand>
        <p>
          Dr. Richardson's staff training at Implant Pathway, robotic placement technology, and
          in-house lab capabilities give Parker-area clients access to our
          <a href="/services/"> full range of dental services</a> at a level found only at specialized
          surgical centers.
        </p>
      </FinalBand>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { initTocSpy } from '../../scripts/toc-spy';
  initTocSpy('.fmdi');
</script>

